  "source": "<section class=\"hero\">\n  <h1 class=\"hero__title\">\n    Fix your Rails app\n    <span class=\"pen-mark\">on the page<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 14\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3 9 C 45 3, 92 12, 138 7 S 214 4, 237 8\"/></svg></span>.\n  </h1>\n  <p class=\"hero__lead\">Edit the text where you see it. Tensaku writes it back to the source.</p>\n  <div class=\"hero__actions\">\n    <a class=\"button button--ink\" href=\"#try\">Try it on this page</a>\n    <a class=\"button\" href=\"/installation\">Install it</a>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"try\" id=\"try\">\n  <ol class=\"try__steps\">\n    <li><strong>Alt-click</strong> the big heading, change a word and press Enter.</li>\n    <li>Press <kbd>Alt</kbd> <kbd>Shift</kbd> <kbd>T</kbd>, click a card below and choose <strong>Add note</strong>.</li>\n    <li>Press <strong>Resolve as the agent</strong> and watch the pin turn green.</li>\n  </ol>\n  <p class=\"try__touch\">On a touch screen, tap 添 in the corner, then Edit.</p>\n</section>\n\n<%= render \"demo/window\" %>\n\n<section class=\"features\">\n  <article>\n    <h3><span class=\"ink-red\">Edit</span> text in place</h3>\n    <p>The editor shows the source. Ruby stays a locked chip, so you only change the words around it.</p>\n  </article>\n  <article>\n    <h3><span class=\"ink-blue\">Notes</span> for your agent</h3>\n    <p>Point at anything and say what should change. Your agent gets the note with the file and line.</p>\n  </article>\n  <article>\n    <h3><span class=\"ink-green\">Production</span> stays the same</h3>\n    <p>Tensaku only loads in development, and every write touches only the bytes you edited.</p>\n  </article>\n</section>\n\n<section class=\"install\">\n  <h2>Two commands</h2>\n  <pre class=\"install__code\"><code>bundle add tensaku --group development\nbin/rails generate tensaku:install</code></pre>\n  <p>Ruby 4.0 and Rails 8.1 or later. <a href=\"/introduction\">Read the docs</a></p>\n</section>\n",
